# The two values a fresh coordinator needs, in the dotenv format the
# Deploy to Cloudflare dialog reads: declaring them here is what makes the
# dialog ask for each value at deploy time and store it as a Worker secret,
# with the descriptions kept in the root package.json's "cloudflare" field.
#
# Locally, `cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars` beside worker/wrangler.toml gives
# `wrangler dev` the same pair. The real file is gitignored; this one ships.
#
# This is deliberately NOT every setting. The sign-in identifiers are [vars]
# in worker/wrangler.toml — public values whose changes should be a reviewable
# diff — and the push secrets are optional and documented in that file's
# secret block. The coordinator refuses to run only with NO way in at all
# (no admin token and no sign-in pair); on a fresh deploy [vars] is empty,
# so these two are what stand between it and that state.
#
# TWO COPIES OF THIS FILE, pinned identical by test/fork-safe-config.test.js:
# this one sits beside the wrangler config, where wrangler's tooling looks,
# and the repository root holds the other, where the deploy button's dialog
# looks — the button hands Cloudflare the whole repository.
AGENT_FLEET_API_TOKEN=""
AGENT_FLEET_AUTH_ALLOW=""
